Z||000000||Bill H||04-29-2001||07:11 PM|||| ok there must be away to make more power with a 3.4. If a 5.7 can make over 500hp then a 3.4 should be capable of 250hp normally asperated. What does it take? Are the 5.7 heads that much better or its intake system that much better? The best figures that I have gotten are 200hp. still real good but 50hp short.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||04-29-2001||07:24 PM||||Hey Bill!<BR>When working on an engine, think of it as an air pump...<BR>The more air it can flow at the same rpm, the more efficient it is...<BR>That is why engine builders use a flow bench, they can test components without building and testing an engine...<BR>BTW, a flow bench is easy to build and use, it just seems like black magic...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||04-29-2001||08:39 PM||||There is WAY more available for the SBC than for the 3.4: intake manifolds, cylinder heads, headers, cams, stud girdles and bottom end parts, etc., etc.<P>If you want power out of a 3.4 and have it be streetable, you need the NEW 3.4 with gen III aluminum heads and roller cam. With ported heads; ported, port-matched and possibly extrude honed intake manifold; port-matched headers; and full roller rockers would almost certainly put it over 200 on the stock cam profile.<BR>||||reg||1
