Z||000008||RedOktober||04-30-2001||02:18 AM||||Just out of curiosity... how much power does one expect to get out of a 0.6 Liter increase in displacement and still using all of the stock Fiero's intake and exhaust plumbing? Stock figure goes something like: 2.8 = 145/150, 3.1 = 165+/_ , 3.4 = 180 .<P>What we really need is better flow through on the heads. the stock valves are of a very good design to get the bottom end torque, but put in some Buick 3.8 Valves in and then we can get better breathing.<BR>or  <BR>Forced induction / NOS / Turbo / V-8 ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Bill H||04-30-2001||07:14 AM|||| Hey Red. the 200hp is with ported and polished heads, intake manifolds, bored t-body, computer chip, and a good free flowing exhaust.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phil||04-30-2001||08:27 AM||||280 HP from SC3800 with small blower pulley.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula88||04-30-2001||09:14 AM||||Check out <A HREF="http://www.grandamgt.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.grandamgt.com</A>  for info on modifying the 3400SFI.  Ram Air Technologies <A HREF="http://www.ramairtech.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ramairtech.com</A>  has parts available to up the factory 175hp (in a Grand Am GT) to about 200, normally aspirated.  Also, this engine has an incredibly flat torque curve, so it feels more powerful than it's peak HP numbers make you think.  Magnuson is alledgedly coming out with a supercharger kit for the 3400SFI that will boost it to about 250-260 HP.  I'd love to use a 3400SFI, but the only drawback is it won't look stock.  If I'm going to put an obviously non-original engine in, why not go for a 3.4 TDC or 3800SC?  Or V8 for that matter...  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||lou_dias||04-30-2001||09:18 AM||||If it's a rebuilt 3.4, you've probably got a compression ratio of 8.9:1...  You need yo bump up the compression to get those extra horses.  Aluminum heads will easily let you go to 10.5:1 on pump fuel...  By the way, 1hp per cubic inch is a fairly smooth and efficient engine so 207hp out of a 3.4 is a good street motor...normally aspirated and on premium pump gas.||||reg||1
